# CHAPTER 3: IN THE HALF-LIGHT, TIME SLOWS DOWN
# Story & Mod by Danish & Pair Programmer

label ch3_main:
    # --- SCENE 1: The Steaming Kettle — 03:55 PM ---
    stop music fadeout 1.5
    scene bg club_sunset
    with dissolve_scene_full

    "After Natsuki slipped out into the corridor, the silence rushed back into the room like water filling an empty glass."

    "I leaned my forehead against the cool glass of the window, watching students walk toward the sports fields below."
    "The bitter cocoa and espresso from Natsuki's cake still lingered on my tongue."
    "A sharp, grounding reminder that I was actually awake, actually here, and not just an avatar living inside a terminal."

    play sound audio.door_open
    pause 0.4

    "The soft click of the classroom door opening broke the quiet."

    "I turned around, half-expecting Sayori's frantic footsteps."
    "Instead, the wooden door slid open with barely a whisper."

    show yuri 1e zorder 2 at t11 with dissolve
    "Yuri stepped inside, carrying her book bag in one arm and a small woven basket in the other."
    "Her dark violet hair cascaded over her shoulder, catching the warm amber light in deep indigo tones."
    "When she saw me sitting by the window, her violet eyes widened slightly with delicate hesitation."

    play sound audio.door_close

    y "\"...Danish?\""
    show yuri 1f at t11
    y "\"I didn't realize anyone was here yet. Am I... interrupting your work?\""

    mc "\"Not at all. I just pushed my last commit about ten minutes ago.\""
    mc "\"You're actually right on time.\""

    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"I see...\""
    show yuri 1f at t11
    y "\"I came up early to prepare the tea before Monika and Sayori arrive.\""
    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"Sayori can be quite enthusiastic, and I find the water requires a measure of patience to reach the proper temperature.\""

    "She set her basket on the desk in the back corner."
    "Out came two ceramic mugs, a matte-black thermos, and a glass canister filled with dried leaves and tiny purple blossoms."

    play music t3

    show yuri 1h at t11
    y "\"Lavender and roasted barley.\""
    show yuri 2d at t11
    y "\"I noticed during our last few meetings that you seemed rather tense.\""
    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"You were rubbing your temples frequently, and your eyes looked strained from your monitors.\""
    show yuri 1f at t11
    y "\"Roasted barley cools the body, and lavender eases tension in the nervous system.\""
    show yuri 1h at t11
    y "\"If... if you wouldn't mind having a cup, that is.\""

    "A sudden lump formed in my throat."
    "First Natsuki with custom espresso ganache, now Yuri with specialized herbal infusions."

    mc "\"Yuri, you really didn't have to do that.\""
    mc "\"You're too good to me.\""

    show yuri 1s at t11
    y "\"It's... it's genuinely no trouble.\""
    show yuri 1v at t11
    y "\"Making tea is a selfish ritual for me, really. It forces the world to stop moving for five minutes while the water heats up.\""
    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"And... lately, it feels as though the world moves far too quickly.\""

    "I let out a low, humorless laugh."

    mc "\"You have no idea how much I needed to hear someone else say that.\""

    # --- SCENE 2: The Amber Corner — 04:05 PM ---
    stop music fadeout 1.5
    scene bg club_sunset
    with dissolve_scene_half

    play music t9

    "We pulled two adjacent student desks together into the sunlit corner of the clubroom."
    "Two mugs steamed between us, releasing a cozy, nutty, floral fragrance."

    show yuri 1a zorder 2 at t11 with dissolve
    "Yuri handed me the ceramic mug with both hands, her slender fingers lightly brushing against mine."
    "The warmth through the clay felt like a physical anchor."

    show yuri 1b at t11
    y "\"Careful. It's quite hot.\""

    "I took a slow sip."
    "The flavor was earthy, roasted, and subtly floral."
    "Not sweet like Natsuki's cake, but grounding."
    "It felt like walking into a warm room after standing out in the rain."

    mc "\"This is amazing. Seriously, Yuri.\""
    mc "\"It feels like my brain just dropped from 100 percent CPU usage down to about 20 percent.\""

    show yuri 1c at h11
    y "\"I'm glad.\""
    show yuri 2m at t11
    y "\"Though... I suspect your brain has been operating at maximum capacity for far too long.\""

    "She rested both hands around her mug, gazing toward the window where the sun cast long shadows across the floorboards."

    show yuri 1f at t11
    y "\"Sayori told me earlier... about today.\""
    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"Happy birthday, Danish.\""

    "I smiled down at the swirling amber liquid in my cup."

    mc "\"Sayori really is incapable of keeping a secret for more than six minutes, isn't she?\""

    show yuri 1d at t11
    y "\"She was extraordinarily excited. She practically cornered me in the library between classes.\""
    show yuri 1h at t11
    y "\"But... she also mentioned that you seemed quiet today. That you were carrying something heavy.\""

    "She turned her head to look at me directly."
    "There was no judgment in her eyes, no demand for an answer—just an open, patient space."

    show yuri 1v at t11
    y "\"If you wish to sit in silence, we can do that. Words are not always necessary.\""
    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"But... if the noise inside your head is becoming suffocating, I am here to listen.\""

    "I took another long sip of tea."
    "I hadn't planned on spilling my guts to anyone today."
    "I had told myself this morning that I would keep my head down and pretend twenty-one was just another integer in a database."
    "Yet sitting here in the quiet glow with Yuri, the armor cracked."

    mc "\"Do you ever feel like you're running on a treadmill that someone keeps speeding up...\""
    mc "\"...and you know you're gonna fall off, but you can't step down because everyone's watching?\""

    show yuri 1u at t11
    "Yuri didn't flinch. Her grip on her mug tightened slightly."

    show yuri 2a at t11
    y "\"Every single day of my life.\""

    # --- SCENE 3: The Vertigo of Tomorrow — 04:15 PM ---
    stop music fadeout 2.0
    scene bg club_dusk
    with dissolve_scene_full

    "Shadows stretched long and thin across the chalkboard."
    "Outside, the amber sky had shifted into deep shades of apricot and violet twilight."

    show yuri 1a zorder 2 at t11 with dissolve
    "I stared down at the dark rim of my mug."

    mc "\"I woke up this morning and looked at my phone. Twenty-one years old.\""
    mc "\"In college, that's supposed to be the year you start feeling like a real adult.\""
    mc "\"All I felt was this sick, heavy panic.\""

    show yuri 1h at t11
    y "\"Because of your internship?\""

    play music t8

    mc "\"Partly. I've been there for a whole year now, since third semester.\""
    mc "\"My boss told me this morning he expects me to renew all the way through semester eight—basically until graduation.\""
    mc "\"On paper, that sounds like a dream, right? People in my classes would kill for that kind of job security.\""

    show yuri 1u at t11
    y "\"But it feels like a cage.\""

    "I looked up, caught off guard by how cleanly she cut straight to the bone."

    mc "\"Yeah. Exactly.\""
    mc "\"It feels like a cage where the bars are made of Jira tickets and Slack pings.\""
    mc "\"If I stay, I spend the next year and a half working forty-hour mental weeks on top of classes, completely exhausted.\""
    mc "\"But if I walk away to breathe? The job market right now is terrifying, Yuri.\""
    mc "\"Tech companies are freezing hiring, laying off thousands, and replacing junior roles with automated pipelines.\""

    "I set the mug down, gesturing with my hands as the frustration bubbled up."

    mc "\"And it's not just the jobs. It's how insanely fast everything is mutating.\""
    mc "\"I love software. I love AI and computers—I really do. But the pace right now is giving me genuine vertigo.\""
    mc "\"Last year, everyone told me to master n8n and workflow automations. I spent weeks wrapping my head around it.\""
    mc "\"Then out of nowhere, OpenClaw drops, and everyone calls the old tools obsolete garbage.\""
    mc "\"Then before anyone can even master OpenClaw, Hermes shows up in less than a year and the entire conversation resets again.\""
    mc "\"Boom. Boom. Boom.\""

    "I leaned forward, resting my elbows on my knees, staring at the floorboards."

    mc "\"It feels like by the time I graduate, every single framework I learned will be useless.\""
    mc "\"And the worst part is the automated coldness of it all.\""
    mc "\"This morning, YouTube banned my second channel out of nowhere. No human reviewed it.\""
    mc "\"No strike, no appeal that gets read by a person. Just an algorithm deciding in a millisecond that my work didn't matter.\""
    mc "\"If algorithms decide what exists, and AI replaces what humans code... what the hell am I even running toward at twenty-one?\""

    "The room fell into a heavy, resonant silence."
    "I waited for the usual empty comfort—the 'you'll be fine' that people give when they don't know what else to say."

    show yuri 1f at t11
    "Yuri didn't offer any of that."
    "She reached into her woven basket and pulled out a hardcover book."

    show book zorder 3 at truecenter with dissolve
    "The cover was bound in muted dark forest green cloth, its spine creased with the gentle wear of someone who had read it many times."
    "Embossed in subtle, faded gold lettering along the spine was '1884'."
    "A slender dark violet ribbon bookmark peeked out from between the antique pages."

    "She placed it gently on the desk between our mugs."
    hide book with dissolve

    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"Do you know when this was written, Danish?\""

    mc "\"The late nineteenth century?\""

    show yuri 1b at t11
    y "\"Eighteen-eighty-four. Over one hundred and forty years ago.\""
    show yuri 1f at t11
    y "\"When the author penned these words, the industrial world was experiencing its own violent acceleration.\""
    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"Steam engines were replacing artisans. Factories were churning out goods faster than human hands ever could.\""
    show yuri 1h at t11
    y "\"People wrote frantic letters to newspapers declaring that poetry was dead...\""
    show yuri 1u at t11
    y "\"...that human craftsmanship was obsolete, and that society was hurling itself into an unfeeling mechanical abyss.\""

    "She opened the cover gently."
    "Tucked inside were small slips of parchment, and in the margins were neat, elegant lines written in dark purple ink."

    stop music fadeout 2.0
    play music t10

    show yuri 1v at t11
    y "\"The machinery of that era has rusted into scrap iron. The steam companies dissolved. The economic panics were forgotten.\""
    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"Yet these words... the fear of isolation, the ache of wanting to be valued, the quiet hope of finding someone who understands your mind...\""
    show yuri 1v at t11
    y "\"They are as alive right now as they were the morning they were printed.\""

    "She looked up, her violet eyes meeting mine with an intensity that made the hair on my arms stand up."

    show yuri 3q at t11
    y "\"Technology moves horizontally, Danish. It expands, it mutates, it accelerates at a speed that is inherently inhuman.\""
    show yuri 1v at t11
    y "\"It will always outpace you if you try to race it on its own terms.\""
    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"But what you bring to it—your curiosity, your frustrations, your love for building things that make people smile...\""
    show yuri 1v at t11
    y "\"That moves vertically. That has depth.\""

    "She gently pushed the book toward me."

    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"You code custom plugins for your games not because an algorithm demanded it, but because you wanted to create something joyful for your friends.\""
    show yuri 1v at t11
    y "\"You worry about your future not because you are lazy, but because you care deeply about doing meaningful work.\""
    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"The world may build faster and faster engines, Danish... but an engine has no purpose without the person who chooses where it travels.\""

    "I stared at the book, then at her."
    "Her cheeks were dusted with crimson, flustered by her own impassioned speech, but she didn't look away."

    show yuri 1j at h11
    y "\"I... I hope that didn't sound too theatrical.\""
    show yuri 1s at t11
    y "\"I only meant... you are not obsolete. You could never be obsolete to the people who know your heart.\""

    "A warm, quiet stillness washed over me."
    "The knot that had been sitting in the center of my chest since dawn finally unraveled."

    mc "\"Yuri... is this for me?\""

    show yuri 1v at t11
    y "\"Yes.\""
    show yuri 2b at t11
    y "\"I selected passages that brought me solace when the world felt too loud. And I wrote a few personal reflections in the margins.\""
    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"You don't have to read it all at once. Just... when you feel the treadmill moving too fast, open a page. And remember to breathe.\""

    # --- SCENE 4: The Secret Ping — 04:30 PM ---
    "Right as I picked up the book to tuck it safely into my bag, the familiar vibration buzzed against my leg."

    play sound audio.phone
    pause 0.4

    "{b}[[Discord - The Boys (KUVART Project)]{/b}\n\"Danish, server endpoint is responding. Clean ping.\""
    "{b}[[Discord - The Boys (KUVART Project)]{/b}\n\"Save your energy for tomorrow's demo call, bro. Don't let your boss run you into the ground.\""

    "A genuine smile tugged at my lips."
    "Good guys."
    "They knew it was my birthday, but instead of making a huge fuss, they just made sure the build was green and told me to rest."

    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"More messages?\""

    mc "\"Yeah. Just the guys from that side project I've been working on.\""

    show yuri 1d at t11
    y "\"Ah... the one Sayori mentioned in passing? She seemed quite convinced it was an international espionage ring.\""

    mc "\"Of course she did. It's called KUVART.\""
    mc "\"It's just a private software project with a few close friends.\""
    mc "\"They're all guys, and they're super paranoid about confidentiality until we actually launch it. That's why I haven't talked about it much.\""
    mc "\"But... they're good people. They keep me grounded when work gets insane.\""

    show yuri 1v at t11
    y "\"I think it's wonderful.\""
    show yuri 1a at t11
    y "\"Having something that belongs entirely to you and your friends... something untouched by corporate metrics.\""
    show yuri 1v at t11
    y "\"You should protect that.\""

    play sound audio.fall
    with hpunch

    "A loud thump violently rattled the classroom door!"

    s "\"Monika, hurry up! I have the streamers! Don't let him leave!\""

    show yuri 1e at h11
    "Yuri and I stared at the shaking door, then looked at each other."

    show yuri 2c at t11
    "Yuri stifled a laugh behind her sleeve, her violet eyes sparkling with amusement."

    y "\"It seems our quiet refuge has come to an end.\""

    mc "\"Yeah.\""
    mc "\"But for once... I think I'm ready for the noise.\""

    stop music fadeout 2.0
    scene black
    with dissolve_scene_full

    pause 2.0

    "{b}End of Chapter 3{/b}\n\nTo be continued in Chapter 4..."

    return
